        "en": {
          "why_it_matters": "The attraction is not an awards pileup so much as the way two very different fiddle voices meet. Carter carries the Del McCoury lineage with a deep sense of bluegrass phrasing and ensemble time; Cleveland brings a huge tone, velocity and a five-string vocabulary that can widen the harmony without leaving the tradition. Their first joint record finally makes that long friendship the center of the music, and The Barns is small enough for bow attack, harmony and rhythmic push-pull to matter physically.",
